<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Merged into the generated bundle by Tauri on macOS.

  LSAppNapIsDisabled: measured, not assumed. On a Mac mini configured never to
  sleep (`pmset`: sleep 0, standby 0, disksleep 0), with the window hidden to
  the tray at 07:19:15, this app's own flight recorder wrote:

      2026-09-10 09:36:42 STALL the process was away for 7753s

  Two hours and nine minutes in which no timer fired, no Announce went out and
  no frame was read - so every contact watching this machine saw it leave, and
  the person opening it from the tray saw grey dots beside peers that had been
  there all along. That is the report this started from ("otwieram z tray na
  macOS - nie ma ikony przy peer linux"), and it was never a bug in the app's
  timers: App Nap suspends a backgrounded process wholesale, and nothing
  written in JavaScript runs during it.

  A messenger with no store-and-forward is unreachable while it is asleep, and
  being reachable IS the reason it sits in the tray. So this app opts out.

  It was NOT the whole story, and this file says so rather than pretending.
  Measured again on 0.5.65, with this key confirmed present in the installed
  bundle (`plutil -extract LSAppNapIsDisabled raw /Applications/onchato.app/
  Contents/Info.plist` -> true) and the machine still set never to sleep:

      2026-09-10 14:43:52 vis hidden
      2026-09-10 14:48:10 5m late=1s          <- still running, five minutes in
      2026-09-10 15:10:56 STALL ... 1129s     <- and back exactly when shown

  Nine minutes after the window was hidden the process was suspended again,
  and it came back in the same second the window was raised. That is the
  OTHER suspect named above, and it is not App Nap: WebKit's own
  `WKPreferences.inactiveSchedulingPolicy` defaults to "suspend", which is
  documented to fully suspend a web view that is not in a window. It is turned
  off in tauri.conf.json (`backgroundThrottling: disabled`, macOS 14+).

  This key stays: App Nap is a separate mechanism with the same consequence,
  and one of them being innocent does not make the other so.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>LSAppNapIsDisabled</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
